regression caught and fixed (H76, PR #198, solo + navigator):
- After H74 merged, `main`'s full `selftest.py` went RED
  (`passed=89 failed=1`): `fn_audit_l3_image` asserted the exact string
  `CORPUS OK: L3 OVERLAY: 0 new / 0 gone / 0 moved`. H74's TODO edit moved 51
  l3 lines, so the gate correctly printed `CORPUS DRIFT: … 0 new / 0 gone /
  51 moved` (exit 0, H69 policy). This is exactly the brittle exact-string
  class H69 removed, re-introduced in a test. The task was created rather than
  silently folded into H75 (rule 9), and — because it edits a standing gate's
  pass/fail assertion — run as a pair even though the block is `Pair: solo`.
  The shipped test accepts `CORPUS (OK|DRIFT): L3 OVERLAY: 0 new / 0 gone /
  N moved` and rejects `CORPUS STALE`; a one-row-deleted overlay still yields
  `CORPUS STALE: 1 new / 0 gone` exit 1, so the assertion is not vacuous.

